# Close the Omni login of anyone whose last working day has passed.
# CFO 2026-09-18: the cut-off is END OF THE LAST WORKING DAY.
#
# TIMING IS LOAD-BEARING, and the obvious choice is wrong. The rule in
# payroll.offboard_access.should_close is `termination_date < today`, so at
# 23:30 on someone's last working day their date is still TODAY and they are
# correctly NOT closed — and the next run is 24 hours later, leaving them open
# all of the following day. Running just after midnight Botswana time is what
# actually delivers "closed at the end of their last day": the date has rolled,
# `< today` is true, and the account shuts about twenty minutes after the last
# day ends. (Caught by the off-subscription review, 2026-09-18.)
#
# Host clock is UTC — verified on the box, `timedatectl` reports Etc/UTC — and
# every other cron here is written in UTC for the same reason.
# 00:20 Botswana (CAT = UTC+2) = 22:20 UTC the previous evening.
#
# Idempotent: an already-closed account is skipped, so a missed night is caught
# the next one. Skips anyone ticked "keep access after exit" (contractors).
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin
20 22 * * * root cd /opt/alpha-finance && docker compose --env-file /etc/alpha-finance/.env exec -T backend python manage.py close_leaver_access >> /var/log/alpha-finance/close-leaver-access.log 2>&1
